<TextPageLayout title="Terms of Service" description="The terms for using SifterSearch, its library, Anís and the API." updated="October 10, 2026" noindex={true}>
  <p>SifterSearch (siftersearch.com) is a non-commercial research tool for an interfaith library, offered by Chad Jones as a
    companion to OceanLibrary.com. By using it you agree to these terms.</p>
  <h2>The library</h2>
  <p>Texts are provided for study and research. Many are in the public domain; others remain under their publishers' or
    authors' rights and are shown for reference. Cite the original source when you quote, and respect any rights notice on a
    document. If you hold rights to a text and want it changed or removed, <a href="/contact">contact us</a>.</p>
  <h2>Anís and other AI features</h2>
  <p>Anís answers from the library using AI models. Answers can be incomplete or wrong; check important matters against
    the cited passages, which are linked so that you can. Nothing here is official guidance of any religious institution.</p>
  <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>No automated bulk downloading or scraping of the site; use the <a href="/docs/api">API</a> within its limits instead.</li>
    <li>No attempts to disrupt the service, get around access controls, or misuse API keys.</li>
    <li>No abusive or unlawful use of the chat or email channels.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Accounts and API keys</h2>
  <p>You are responsible for activity under your account and keys. We may suspend access that breaks these terms.</p>
  <h2>No warranty</h2>
  <p>The service is provided "as is", without warranties of any kind, and may change or stop at any time. To the extent the
    law allows, we are not liable for losses arising from its use.</p>
  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>We may update these terms; the date above shows the latest version. See also the <a href="/privacy">Privacy notice</a>.</p>
